    "summary": "Mellow Providence ’82 – Scarlet > Fire & Morning Dew sparkle on a clear matrix",
    "review": "The April 15, 1982 Providence Civic Center gig is a solid example of the early‑‘80s Dead: a first set that drifts by with respectable workman‑like playing and a second set that really lifts off. The highlight reel kicks off with a smooth Scarlet Begonias → Fire on the Mountain segue that feels both relaxed and purposeful, then rolls into an inspired Estimated Prophet → He’s Gone stretch before Bill and Mickey lock in tight with Brent’s lush keyboards for a drum/keyboard‑driven interlude. The set closes with a beautifully rendered Morning Dew that lets Brent’s piano sing over Jerry’s warm lead lines. While the show never reaches the fireworks of a ‘77 spring run, it offers the kind of understated magic that makes 1982 fans smile – especially when heard on the well‑mastered matrix recording.\n\nIf you’re hunting a clean listening experience, the matrix tape (gd1982-04-15.set2.sonyECM220t.kirschner.miller.95434) delivers crystal‑clear 24‑bit/96 kHz sound with no drop‑outs, letting every nuance of Brent’s keyboard work and Bill’s drum interplay shine. It captures the second‑set flow perfectly, making this the go‑to source for anyone wanting to hear Providence at its mellow best.",
